UID:10005854-1795219200-1795391999@sdlancaster.org
SUMMARY:MHS Fall Play
DESCRIPTION:A journey to Neverland awaits as the McCaskey Visual & Performing Arts Department presents its fall play\, “Peter Pan & Wendy\,” Nov. 21 and 22 at McCaskey East. Adapted by Lauren Gunderson from J.M. Barrie’s classic story\, the production follows the Darling children into a world of adventure while offering a fresh perspective on the familiar tale. With humor and imagination\, the play explores friendship\, courage and what it means to find your own voice. \nThe production gives the Lancaster community an opportunity to enjoy live theater while supporting McCaskey’s student performers and artists. Families with younger children have an added invitation to attend. School District of Lancaster elementary students will receive free admission with the purchase of an adult ticket. \nPerformances will take place at 7 p.m. Nov. 21 and 2 p.m. Nov. 22 in the McCaskey East auditorium\, 1051 Lehigh Ave. Lancaster. \nTickets are $10 for community members and $7 for students. \nJoin our students for a trip to Neverland and help fill the auditorium for a weekend of theater at McCaskey. \n  \nPURCHASE TICKETS HERE: https://cur8.com/15286/project/141879 
URL:https://sdlancaster.org/event/mhs-fall-play-2/
LOCATION:East Auditorium\, 1051 Lehigh Avenue\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602
CATEGORIES:McCaskey HS
END:VEVENT
